=== REASONING (approach + alternatives rejected) ===

GOAL: bring Apple unit coverage to the ADR-010 bar AND run the exact 5-part gate
green (iOS build+test, macOS build+test, swiftlint --strict, swiftformat --lint,
check-placeholders). Coverage code already exists at scale, so the work reduced to
(a) clearing the host gates honestly and (b) getting the build+test legs to run.

PLACEHOLDER GATE FIX (host gate, in Allowed-Files):
  - For the 85 short lines: appended `// parity:allow <reason>` (the gate's designed,
    reason-required opt-out) with accurate per-category reasons (em-dash fallback /
    web i18n key / input prompt / loading skeleton / ui copy / test name), each kept
    <=120 chars so swiftlint line_length (warn 120, --strict) and swiftformat
    wrapSingleLineComments (maxwidth 120) both still pass.
  - For 6 long doc-comments where no marker could fit <=120: reworded "placeholder"
    to the accurate term it denotes (template `tokens`, loading `skeletons`, input
    `prompt`, `fallback`) — matching the codebase convention (LiveMotorStatus.Adapter
    notes surfaces use `emDash`/`fallback` "never 'placeholder', so [they] carr[y] no
    ADR-011 markers"). No marker needed; line shortens.
  - For 2 long code lines (an i18n-key assertion + an em-dash ChargePlanBadge arg):
    wrapped the call per swiftformat --wraparguments before-first style.
  REJECTED: blanket renaming every `placeholder` identifier (broad cross-file blast
  radius, compile risk) and blanket comment substitution (semantically lossy — the
  word means 5 different things across the hits). The chosen mix is accurate + minimal.

PREDECESSOR COMPILE FIXES (needed for the build leg to even start; in Allowed-Files):
  - 3x "escaping closure captures non-escaping parameter 'content'" — added `@escaping`
    to `glass(@ViewBuilder _ content:)` in AIAutoNameUnnamedLocations / AISignalExplorerNlFilter
    / AIGeofenceAwareAutomationSuggestions, matching the 7 sibling surfaces that already
    have it (TSGlassPanel.init takes `@escaping`).
  - 1x "compiler unable to type-check this expression in reasonable time" —
    RecentDrivesSection.Previews.swift:24: split a mixed Int/Double literal-inference
    `.map { … }` into explicitly-typed locals.
  These are correct, convention-aligned fixes. They are NOT a "fix" for the blocker
  below — they merely let compilation PROCEED far enough to hit it.

BLOCKER (intractable here): a deterministic Swift 6.3.2 IRGen COMPILER CRASH — see GATE.
